Ideally someone will create a Firefox extension for a right-click menu
item on highlighted Lojban text to get word lookup, or even jbofi'e.
Even better would be right-click menu item on highlighted English text
to see a set of suggestions of Lojban words that might-- just might--
apply or contribute to translating English words, with the user urged
to use his or her judgement.

My super-convenient tool of choice, although not as shiny as what you
described, is a drop-down menu of bookmarks in Firefox. Your mileage
may vary. Apologies to those who have seen me post this here before.

Go to the Bookmarks menu and select "Manage Bookmarks". Create a
folder called Lojban and drag it into the Bookmarks Toolbar Folder.
Bookmark the following sites in that folder:

http://www.lojban.org/jboski/
http://www.hypermetrics.com/pikmin.html
http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/
http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/gismu.txt
http://www.lojban.org/publications/wordlists/cmavo.txt
